  "locus": "Theses in quibus exponitur Doctrina Scholae Romanae circa partitionem Gratiae in sufficientem atque efficacem, & concordiam libertatis humanae cum Gratiae efficacia, CXVI-CXXIV (the middle way of Bellarmine, Vasquez and Petrus a Sancto Joseph between Molina and the recent Thomists: with Molina, sufficient grace that suffices for actual conversion if one wills (Petrus a Sancto Joseph, De gratia divina disp. 6 sect. 6; Idea theologiae speculativae 4.7), and no physical predetermination, though grace moves the will physically like an impressed impetus (disp. 7); efficacious grace placed in the same illuminations and affections as Molina's; but its efficacy not from consent: the will consents because grace is efficacious (Bellarmine, De gratia et libero arbitrio 1.12; De gratia divina disp. 7 sect. 9 num. 61)).",
